# GUARD settings-save-refusal-is-reported
#
# `writeConfigTheme` was documented as "silent at every failure" and it was.
# Against a config file at mode 0444 the settings panel announced the path it
# saves to, return applied the theme live, the panel closed, nothing was
# written, and nothing anywhere said so -- no band, no changed line, no log the
# user can see. The disagreement between the running app and the file only
# surfaced at the next launch, as a theme that reverted for no visible reason.
#
# The break puts that silence back, and only that. It leaves the model plumbing
# (`ConfigWrite`, `config_write_refused`, `Settings.config_writable`,
# `configFileWritable`) in place so the tree still COMPILES -- a break that
# stops compilation exits non-zero for the wrong reason and proves nothing --
# and removes the two lines that make the plumbing reach a person: the latch in
# `persistThemeChoice` and the writability probe in `settings_open`. Every
# conditional downstream then reads its default, which is exactly the old
# behaviour: "saves to <path>", unqualified, and no band afterwards.
#
# The test fails at the FIRST of the two halves it asserts, the panel line, so
# a red run names line 379 rather than the latch. The latch half was proved red
# on its own as well, with the `persistThemeChoice` hunk of this patch applied
# alone: `config_write_refused` stays false through a commit the file refused.
test: a config file that refuses the write is reported, not swallowed
red: 2026-08-15 at 0c34cc1
diff --git a/src/cockpit/update.zig b/src/cockpit/update.zig
